                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="1656-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_o.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Omnidirectional" title="Omnidirectional" ><img id="1656-1" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ></span>Microphone Parts RA-23</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Multi-Pattern Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The RA-23 is a dual-pattern FET condenser that was sold as a DIY microphone kit. It has since been repackaged and renamed for the type of capsule included; the new versions (as of 2015) are called the S-47, S-12, and S-87.</p><p><a rel="shadowbox" href="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images//mic_extras/mparts/RA23-xray.jpg"><img src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/mic_extras/mparts/RA23-xray-sm.jpg" class="thumb shaft" alt="RA-23 Cutaway View" width="200" /></a>The kit includes a transformerless circuit based on the Schoeps CMC-5. The two PCBs are made in the USA. The components include matched capacitors, specially selected and pre-biased Siliconix J305 JFET, low-noise Hitachi output transistors (also matched), and precision resistors.</p><p>The PCBs were designed to fit easily with the enclosed body, which is aluminum (anodized in black), with a tapered grille made of 2 layers of brass mesh. The use of two layers of different-gauge mesh offers a good compromise between plosive protection (in which more layers are beneficial), resonance reduction (ditto), and minimization of sonic reflections (in which fewer layers, and a more open weave would be preferred).</p><p>Any of 5 large-diaphragm capsules can be selected, including K47, K67, and CK-12 types. The capsule choice affects sensitivity and frequency response, but in all cases the sensitivity would be at least 27mV/Pa (and possibly as high as 45mV/Pa), and self-noise would be below 13dBA.</p><p>The polar pattern switch on the PCB removes the capsule&#8217;s rear diaphragm from the circuit entirely when in &#8220;True Cardioid&#8221; mode; this raises the sensitivity of the mic by ~4dB in Cardioid as compared to Omni.</p><p>The kit includes: microphone chassis and body, capsule mount, capsule, PCBs (unpopulated), all components necessary to build the circuit, US-made silver/teflon hookup wire, and a zippered storage pouch.<p>Permalink: <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Microphone-Parts/RA-23">Microphone Parts RA-23</a></p><p>The mic was released in 2014.</p>
